Shipped a production-polished, native Apple-idiomatic **`Toggle`** shared surface at parity with `web/src/components/ui/Toggle.tsx`, following the established `Slider` (0226) predecessor pattern.

**9 files created** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Toggle.*`), committed as `776e82c33`:
- `Toggle.Adapter.swift` — pure core: i18n `Resolve` seam, `Meta`, `Size` (sm/md→ControlSize), `Input` snapshot, `Accessibility` builder
- `Toggle.Projection.swift` — `ToggleResolved` + pure projection
- `Toggle.Model.swift` — P1/S8 `@Observable @MainActor` state-holder, P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry seam, P1/S10 strings facade
- `Toggle.Views.swift` / `Toggle.swift` — native `SwiftUI.Toggle(.switch)` + trailing tappable label; public `ToggleSwitch` view (named to avoid shadowing `SwiftUI.Toggle`)
- `Toggle.Previews.swift`, `Toggle.strings`, `Toggle.Tests.swift`, `Toggle.AdapterTests.swift`

**Design fidelity:** reproduces the web's genuine branches — on/off, optional label (+label-tap toggle), and sm/md size. Like the source (a controlled `checked`/`useId` primitive with no fetch), there is no loading/error/stale/offline axis; inventing one would be fabricating state — the predecessor-accepted disposition.

